      "writtenOn": "2026-10-19T09:45:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am now feeling that ,we should have automated tests for year, month, day, and second resolutions, as well as positive/negative UTC offsets, unspecified UTC, null resolution, and invalid length. Coarse resolution cases would catch the formatting issue above.\n\nWhen we started the project pldmtool was very tiny, and was just a developer only tool to test only the bmc pldm stack. Now that this has been instrumental in catching issues even from devices \u0026 pldm stack has been scaled to various companies , i think its time to get the tests added.",
      "revId": "ad448cbffe946c69120b5bc85c452b747a255973",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
